{
 "id": "action-cam-mount-petg",
 "brief": "An action-camera mount base in PETG on an FDM printer (choose the print orientation): the three-finger side of the usual two-and-three finger joint. The joint's M5 bolt runs along Y through the origin. The three fingers are 3 mm thick, 15 mm round about the bolt, at y = -7.6 to -4.6, -1.5 to 1.5 and 4.6 to 7.6, and the two slots between them must stay clear out to 9.5 mm from the bolt so the mating fingers can swing. The base is a 32 mm square plate, z = -20 to -16, held down by four M3 screws at (+-12, +-12) into the surface under it. Everything stays inside the plate's footprint between z = -20 and z = -8, plus the fingers above. The camera on its pole puts up to 50 N on the joint 60 mm above the bolt, along X or along Y. Safety factor 2.5.",
